{"resource":{"id":"go-sample-exercises","title":"Go — Sample Exercises","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"22 min","pages":20,"lastUpdated":"June 2026","tags":["Programming","Go","Concurrency"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"A concept-wise Go workbook — 200+ short exercises across syntax, structs, interfaces, goroutines, channels, files, JSON, APIs, and backend basics."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Syntax Practice"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Functions"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Structs & Interfaces"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Goroutines"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Channels"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. File Handling"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. JSON"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. HTTP & APIs"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Debugging"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Mini Projects"},{"id":"s11","label":"11. Reflection Questions"},{"id":"review","label":"Exercise Review"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Go — Practice Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"31 min"},{"title":"Go — Beginner Guide","tag":"Programming","time":"17 min"},{"title":"Go — Complete Tutorial","tag":"Programming","time":"55 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Reinforce every core Go concept with short, focused exercises.</li>\n          <li>Progress from syntax to backend fundamentals over ~4 weeks.</li>\n          <li>Practice reflection — <em>why</em> each solution works, not just <em>how</em>.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"/><path d=\"M9 18h6\"/><path d=\"M10 22h4\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Format</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Each block below has 15–25 exercises. Spend 20 minutes on each concept, note stumbles, revisit later.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Syntax Practice</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm\">\n          <li>Print your name in three ways: <code>fmt.Print</code>, <code>Println</code>, <code>Printf</code>.</li>\n          <li>Declare 5 constants of different types.</li>\n          <li>Swap two variables without a temporary.</li>\n          <li>Compute Fahrenheit from Celsius for -40..100 in steps of 10.</li>\n          <li>Read a number from stdin and print its square.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Functions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm\">\n          <li>Write <code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>abs</code> for ints.</li>\n          <li>Variadic average of any number of floats.</li>\n          <li>Closure that returns an incrementing counter.</li>\n          <li>Recursive factorial + iterative version — compare.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Structs &amp; Interfaces</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>type Shape interface { Area() float64 }\n// Implement Rect and Circle satisfying Shape.</code></pre></div>\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm\">\n          <li>Model a <code>Book</code> with methods to format its citation.</li>\n          <li>Compose <code>Address</code> into <code>Employee</code> via embedding.</li>\n          <li>Implement <code>fmt.Stringer</code> on your <code>User</code>.</li>\n        </ol>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Composition over inheritance: build up types by embedding smaller ones.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Goroutines</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm\">\n          <li>Launch 5 goroutines that print their id.</li>\n          <li>Sum a slice concurrently with <code>sync.WaitGroup</code>.</li>\n          <li>Detect leaks by counting <code>runtime.NumGoroutine()</code> before/after.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Channels</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>ch := make(chan int)\ngo func(){ for i := 1; i &lt;= 5; i++ { ch &lt;- i }; close(ch) }()\nfor v := range ch { fmt.Println(v) }</code></pre></div>\n        <p>Extend it to a bounded pipeline with a middle transformation stage.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. File Handling</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm\">\n          <li>Copy a file byte-by-byte using <code>bufio</code>.</li>\n          <li>Read a CSV and print unique columns.</li>\n          <li>Write a struct as JSON to disk and read it back.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. JSON</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>type User struct{ Name string \\`json:&quot;name&quot;\\`; Age int \\`json:&quot;age,omitempty&quot;\\` }</code></pre></div>\n        <p>Marshal and unmarshal collections; test omitting <code>Age</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. HTTP &amp; APIs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm\">\n          <li>Build a <code>/health</code> endpoint returning JSON.</li>\n          <li>Add a <code>/echo</code> endpoint that reflects request headers.</li>\n          <li>Middleware that logs latency for every request.</li>\n        </ol>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Request lifecycle: middleware → handler → service → repository → response.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Debugging</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Introduce common bugs (nil map, unclosed channel, goroutine leak) into your own code — then reproduce, isolate, and fix them under a stopwatch.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Mini Projects</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Todo CLI storing JSON on disk.</li>\n          <li>Concurrent web fetcher with a worker pool.</li>\n          <li>Static file server with directory listings.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Reflection Questions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm\">\n          <li>Which chapter felt hardest? Why?</li>\n          <li>What idiom surprised you compared to your previous language?</li>\n          <li>What would you refactor after another read of the standard library?</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"review\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Exercise Review</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold\">Progress Tracker</h3>\n        <p>Aim for 15 exercises per weekday for 4 weeks.</p>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Learning Checklist</h3>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>✅ Comfortable with slices, maps, structs.</li>\n          <li>✅ Wrote at least one goroutine + channel pipeline.</li>\n          <li>✅ Built a working HTTP handler.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Practice Schedule</h3>\n        <p>Alternate concepts weekly — never spend 5 days on one chapter.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Where are the answers?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Solutions for equivalent problems live in the Answer Key resource; this workbook is deliberately open-ended.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>How much time per day?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">45–90 minutes is ideal — enough to focus, small enough to stay consistent.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Idiom</strong> — a pattern the community considers canonical.</li>\n          <li><strong>Refactor</strong> — improve code shape without changing behaviour.</li>\n          <li><strong>Regression</strong> — a bug that returns after being fixed.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n          Exercises for self-paced practice. Verify solutions against official documentation and\n          community linters. Trademarks belong to their respective owners.\n        </p>\n      </div></section>"}